 asia and china has been changed  through these years and that could be  part of the reason  why xinjiang didn't make any profit  many countries stopped seeking  replacement  of traditional full cell energy  replacing them  with renewable energy such as solar  the coronal coronavirus outbreak is just  the trigger  always collapsed the founder of  homegrown  oil trading firm hindiang trading has  been charged with amendment of forgery  for the purpose of cheating  lim un quinn allegedly asked an employee  to forge  a document to state that kin liang had  transferred more than one  million barrels of gas oil to china  aviation oil corporation  this document was allegedly used to  secure almost 77  million dollars in trade funds from a  financial institution  if found guilty lim could be jailed for  up to 10 years and fined  king liang and lims is one of the most  secretive family business in singapore  multiple attempts  to henyang and ling's family for  comments  went unsuccessful so after the hindiang  episode  when some banks found themselves with  hundreds of millions of dollars of  losses  we're seeing that the oil industry in  asia is going through  somewhat of an evolution where smaller  companies are finding it harder to get  credit lines and financing and even  bigger companies more reputable  companies  are also finding that credit lines are  being shrunken  [Music]  you

